<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grantley Adams</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1898–1971</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grantley Adams was a Barbadian lawyer and labour leader who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbados-labour-party">Barbados Labour Party</a> and pushed through labour and electoral reforms after the riots of 1937. He became the island's first premier and was the only prime minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> Federation from 1958 until its dissolution in 1962. He is a National Hero of Barbados.</p></div>
